# How a traced corpus is actually built

Recovered from git history on 2026-08-09, after the derivers were found missing
and a first attempt to regenerate produced 56,938 rows against the 56,875 on
disk with not one row matching.

The reason it did not match is that **a traced corpus is not deriver output.**

## The chain

```
<model>-grounded.finetune.jsonl          the source pairs
        │
        ▼  asc_soma.derive.<model>     deterministic, free, no teacher
   derived traces                        --repair-pct 15 --direct-pct 20
        │
        ▼  asc_soma.teacher.merge_all_cached_traces
   bought teacher traces merged over it, by priority
        │
        ▼
<model>-traced.finetune.jsonl
```

## The flags, recovered

From `kernel_asc_dsl_v3.py` at `9caf8dd4`:

```
derive_traces.py --in  <model>-grounded.finetune.jsonl
                 --out <model>-traced.finetune.jsonl
                 --repair-pct 15
                 --direct-pct 20
```

Those are the defaults, which is why the flags were never the discrepancy.

## Teacher priority, which is load-bearing

`merge_all_cached_traces.MODELS` is an ordered list and the order is the
priority. Luna leads because it is the strongest teacher run and the one whose
traces were bought deliberately; the rest are fallbacks for rows Luna never saw.

A row that already has a trace **keeps** it. That rule was added at `6db19055`
after the merge was found to be replacing rather than filling: 2,480 query rows,
5,024 form-extract and 1,016 asc-dsl had been quietly demoted from Luna to
kimi, which is the exact opposite of the stated priority. The tool can identify
the teacher of a trace it looks up and never of one already in the corpus, so
replacing means overwriting an unknown teacher with a known one.

## What survived and what did not

**Survived.** The teacher caches, 94 MB at
`packages/ai-corpus/data/soma-train/teacher/`, committed deliberately at
`90a97774` as "the paid-for artefact". The five derivers, restored to
`asc_soma/derive/`. The five teacher tools, restored to `asc_soma/teacher/`.

**Does not run yet.** The teacher tools import `soma_paths`, `domains` and the
old `soma` model module, all deleted with the harness. Rewiring those three is
what stands between here and regenerating a traced corpus from source.

## Why this file exists

The corpora were checked in and the recipe was not. That is the same failure as
the derivers being deleted, one level up, and it cost an afternoon to undo. A
derive stage should write its own parameters into the artefact manifest so this
document becomes redundant.
